{
  "schema": "loom.runtime_profile/1",
  "domain": "chat_context",
  "revision": 1,
  "description": "Order of context classes in the chat prompt and the selector profiles. Orders: legacy reproduces the historical order byte for byte (system, memory, graph, project, history); stable_first puts the slowly changing classes first so provider prompt prefixes stay reusable (system, memory, project, history, graph); stability (the default preset since M1-D2) adds the classes profile (the stable part of what the app knows about the user) and rules (the rules about the user) right after the system instruction: system, profile, rules, memory, project, history, graph. The active-task block and the question always come last. Since work item M1-K1a the kernel fills them: rules is the standing rules about the person (under the orders without this class they stay in the instruction part, as before), profile is what the person told about themselves, rendered by profile_prefix. Both are empty when there is nothing to send, and then stability sends the same bytes as stable_first. Orders are data: a user can add their own named order. selector_profiles are the presets of the context selector (a view kind of the same name): each is a bundle of knobs that already exist, not a new engine. In a profile a null number or name means: what the setting says now (graph_memory_max_nodes, graph_memory_depth, chat_representation, chat_flow); a source set to false is not read by that profile; a number of a source that is false is 0 and ignored; history_window null = the whole conversation; budget_tokens null = no limit of its own. profile_prefix is the recipe of the class profile: a fixed header, a fixed line format, the subgraphs of the node You (profile.subgraphs in user.pack, sorted by order_for_prefix) and which of them (and which keys) each profile_detail_level carries. Presets, not rules.",
  "defaults": {
    "context_order": "stability",
    "orders": {
      "legacy": [
        "system",
        "memory",
        "graph",
        "project",
        "history"
      ],
      "stable_first": [
        "system",
        "memory",
        "project",
        "history",
        "graph"
      ],
      "stability": [
        "system",
        "profile",
        "rules",
        "memory",
        "project",
        "history",
        "graph"
      ]
    },
    "selector_profiles": [
      {
        "id": "loom",
        "label": {
          "pl": "ChatADHD (preset)",
          "en": "ChatADHD (preset)"
        },
        "why": {
          "pl": "Zwykły czat z pełnym kontekstem: instrukcja, to, co wiem o Tobie, reguły o Tobie, pamięć, projekt, rozmowa i powiązania z grafu. Początek żądania jest taki sam w każdej turze, więc dostawca może go zapamiętać i bywa taniej.",
          "en": "A normal chat with the full context: the instruction, what I know about you, the rules about you, memory, project, the conversation and the links from the graph. The start of the request is the same in every turn, so the provider can remember it and it can be cheaper."
        },
        "order": "stability",
        "sources": {
          "profile": true,
          "rules": true,
          "memory": true,
          "project": true,
          "history": true,
          "graph": true,
          "search": false,
          "kb": false
        },
        "breadth": {
          "nodes": null,
          "search_limit": 0,
          "history_window": null
        },
        "depth": {
          "hops": null
        },
        "representation": null,
        "flow": null,
        "budget_tokens": null,
        "status": "preset",
        "note": {
          "pl": "Liczba węzłów i głębokość grafu, sposób wysłania rozmowy i przepływ są takie, jak w ustawieniach (preset: 20 węzłów, głębokość 2). Jądro stosuje ten profil: porządek „stability”, źródła i liczby z tabeli (tu: jak w ustawieniach) oraz sposób wysłania rozmowy. Część „Profil” zawiera tylko to, co sam powiedziałeś o sobie w wywiadzie; bez wywiadu jest pusta i żądanie jest takie jak w porządku „stable_first”.",
          "en": "The number of graph nodes, the depth, how the conversation is sent and the flow are as in the settings (preset: 20 nodes, depth 2). The kernel applies this profile: the order “stability”, the sources and the numbers of the table (here: as in the settings) and how the conversation is sent. The part “Profile” holds only what you said about yourself in the interview; without an interview it is empty and the request is the same as with the order “stable_first”."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "loom_legacy",
        "label": {
          "pl": "ChatADHD (dawny)",
          "en": "ChatADHD (legacy)"
        },
        "why": {
          "pl": "Tak jak było przed zmianą: dokładnie te same bajty żądania, bez części o Tobie. Do powrotu, gdy coś ma wyglądać jak dawniej.",
          "en": "As it was before the change: exactly the same request bytes, without the part about you. For going back when something must look as it did."
        },
        "order": "legacy",
        "sources": {
          "profile": false,
          "rules": true,
          "memory": true,
          "project": true,
          "history": true,
          "graph": true,
          "search": false,
          "kb": false
        },
        "breadth": {
          "nodes": null,
          "search_limit": 0,
          "history_window": null
        },
        "depth": {
          "hops": null
        },
        "representation": null,
        "flow": null,
        "budget_tokens": null,
        "status": "preset",
        "note": {
          "pl": "Instrukcja, pamięć, graf, projekt, historia; reguły strażnika są w części z instrukcją, bez prefiksu profilu. Ten sam efekt daje dziś ustawienie „Kolejność części żądania” = legacy. Jądro stosuje ten profil: bajty żądania są dokładnie dawne (pilnuje tego test ze złotym plikiem).",
          "en": "The instruction, memory, graph, project, history; the guardian rules sit in the instruction part, without the profile prefix. The same effect is given today by the setting “Order of the request parts” = legacy. The kernel applies this profile: the request bytes are exactly the old ones (a test with a golden file guards it)."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "compat",
        "label": {
          "pl": "Zgodność",
          "en": "Compatibility"
        },
        "why": {
          "pl": "Tylko stała instrukcja i cała rozmowa, jak w zwykłym czacie u dostawcy. Bez pamięci, grafu i tego, co wiem o Tobie. Do porównań i gdy dodatki przeszkadzają.",
          "en": "Only the fixed instruction and the whole conversation, as in a plain provider chat. Without memory, the graph and what I know about you. For comparisons and when the extras get in the way."
        },
        "order": "legacy",
        "sources": {
          "profile": false,
          "rules": false,
          "memory": false,
          "project": false,
          "history": true,
          "graph": false,
          "search": false,
          "kb": false
        },
        "breadth": {
          "nodes": 0,
          "search_limit": 0,
          "history_window": null
        },
        "depth": {
          "hops": 0
        },
        "representation": "raw",
        "flow": "plain",
        "budget_tokens": null,
        "status": "preset",
        "note": {
          "pl": "Surowa rozmowa w całości (bez okna historii), bez pamięci, projektu, grafu, profilu i reguł. Jądro stosuje ten profil w całości.",
          "en": "The raw conversation in full (no history window), without memory, project, graph, profile and rules. The kernel applies this profile in full."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "lean",
        "label": {
          "pl": "Oszczędny",
          "en": "Economical"
        },
        "why": {
          "pl": "Jak ChatADHD, ale rozmowa bez wypełniaczy i dygresji, a pamięć z grafu płytsza i mniejsza. Mniej tokenów w każdej turze.",
          "en": "Like ChatADHD, but the conversation without fillers and digressions, and the graph memory shallower and smaller. Fewer tokens in every turn."
        },
        "order": "stability",
        "sources": {
          "profile": true,
          "rules": true,
          "memory": true,
          "project": true,
          "history": true,
          "graph": true,
          "search": false,
          "kb": false
        },
        "breadth": {
          "nodes": 10,
          "search_limit": 0,
          "history_window": null
        },
        "depth": {
          "hops": 1
        },
        "representation": "lean",
        "flow": null,
        "budget_tokens": null,
        "status": "preset",
        "note": {
          "pl": "Twoje wiadomości bez wypełniaczy i dygresji (poziom L2 z analizy, tam gdzie jest). Graf: 10 węzłów i 1 skok to liczby presetu, można je zmienić. Jądro stosuje ten profil w całości; poziom L2 jest użyty tam, gdzie analiza go zapisała, a gdzie nie ma, idzie tekst surowy.",
          "en": "Your messages without fillers and digressions (level L2 of the analysis, where it exists). Graph: 10 nodes and 1 hop are preset numbers, you can change them. The kernel applies this profile in full; level L2 is used where the analysis wrote it, and the raw text goes where it did not."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "graph_in",
        "label": {
          "pl": "Graf na wejściu",
          "en": "Graph in"
        },
        "why": {
          "pl": "Wybrany kontekst idzie do modelu jako pakiet grafu (węzły i powiązania), głębiej niż zwykle. Odpowiedź może być tekstem albo grafem.",
          "en": "The chosen context goes to the model as a graph packet (nodes and links), deeper than usual. The answer can be text or a graph."
        },
        "order": "stability",
        "sources": {
          "profile": true,
          "rules": true,
          "memory": true,
          "project": true,
          "history": true,
          "graph": true,
          "search": false,
          "kb": false
        },
        "breadth": {
          "nodes": null,
          "search_limit": 0,
          "history_window": null
        },
        "depth": {
          "hops": 3
        },
        "representation": null,
        "flow": "graph_in",
        "budget_tokens": null,
        "status": "calibration",
        "note": {
          "pl": "Kalibracja: w 12 wywołaniach mechanika zadziałała 12/12, cel 10/12, pełna adekwatność 9/12, oparcie w źródłach 9/12 (docs/reports/model-research-2026-10-04.md:21). Głębokość 3 to wartość wyjściowa do strojenia. Jądro stosuje ten profil w całości (głębokość 3 i przepływ graph_in).",
          "en": "Calibration: in 12 calls the mechanics worked 12/12, the goal 10/12, full adequacy 9/12, grounding in the sources 9/12 (docs/reports/model-research-2026-10-04.md:21). Depth 3 is a starting value to tune. The kernel applies this profile in full (depth 3 and the flow graph_in)."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "like_claude",
        "label": {
          "pl": "Jak Claude (apka)",
          "en": "Like Claude (app)"
        },
        "why": {
          "pl": "Na początku to, co wiem o Tobie (styl i preferencje), potem pamięć projektu i rozmowa. Bez grafu.",
          "en": "First what I know about you (style and preferences), then the project memory and the conversation. Without the graph."
        },
        "order": "stability",
        "sources": {
          "profile": true,
          "rules": false,
          "memory": true,
          "project": true,
          "history": true,
          "graph": false,
          "search": false,
          "kb": false
        },
        "breadth": {
          "nodes": 0,
          "search_limit": 0,
          "history_window": null
        },
        "depth": {
          "hops": 0
        },
        "representation": "raw",
        "flow": "plain",
        "budget_tokens": null,
        "status": "calibration",
        "note": {
          "pl": "Kalibracja: to nasze przybliżenie, nie odtworzenie; dokładne odtworzenie i testy porównawcze są w etapie replikacji. Artefakty i narzędzia tej aplikacji: planowane. Jądro stosuje ten profil w całości.",
          "en": "Calibration: this is our approximation, not a replica; the exact replication and comparative tests belong to the replication stage. The artifacts and tools of that app: planned. The kernel applies this profile in full."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "like_chatgpt",
        "label": {
          "pl": "Jak ChatGPT (apka)",
          "en": "Like ChatGPT (app)"
        },
        "why": {
          "pl": "Własne instrukcje z tego, co wiem o Tobie, odpowiednie wpisy z pamięci, kilka najlepiej pasujących fragmentów dawnych rozmów i bieżąca rozmowa.",
          "en": "Custom instructions from what I know about you, the fitting memory entries, a few of the best matching passages of past conversations and the current conversation."
        },
        "order": "stability",
        "sources": {
          "profile": true,
          "rules": true,
          "memory": true,
          "project": false,
          "history": true,
          "graph": false,
          "search": true,
          "kb": false
        },
        "breadth": {
          "nodes": 0,
          "search_limit": 10,
          "history_window": null
        },
        "depth": {
          "hops": 0
        },
        "representation": "raw",
        "flow": "plain",
        "budget_tokens": null,
        "status": "calibration",
        "note": {
          "pl": "Kalibracja: to nasze przybliżenie, nie odtworzenie; dokładne odtworzenie i testy porównawcze są w etapie replikacji. 10 wyników szukania to liczba presetu. Jądro stosuje ten profil poza szukaniem w historii rozmów (search_limit), którego jeszcze nie ma; reszta działa.",
          "en": "Calibration: this is our approximation, not a replica; the exact replication and comparative tests belong to the replication stage. 10 search results is a preset number. The kernel applies this profile except the search through past conversations (search_limit), which does not exist yet; the rest works."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "like_gemini",
        "label": {
          "pl": "Jak Gemini (apka)",
          "en": "Like Gemini (app)"
        },
        "why": {
          "pl": "Kanał „kontekst osobisty”: najlepiej pasujące fragmenty dawnych rozmów i bieżąca rozmowa. Bez pamięci i grafu.",
          "en": "A “personal context” channel: the best matching passages of past conversations and the current conversation. Without memory and the graph."
        },
        "order": "stability",
        "sources": {
          "profile": false,
          "rules": false,
          "memory": false,
          "project": false,
          "history": true,
          "graph": false,
          "search": true,
          "kb": false
        },
        "breadth": {
          "nodes": 0,
          "search_limit": 10,
          "history_window": null
        },
        "depth": {
          "hops": 0
        },
        "representation": "raw",
        "flow": "plain",
        "budget_tokens": null,
        "status": "calibration",
        "note": {
          "pl": "Kalibracja: to nasze przybliżenie, nie odtworzenie; dokładne odtworzenie i testy porównawcze są w etapie replikacji. 10 wyników szukania to liczba presetu. Jądro stosuje ten profil poza szukaniem w historii rozmów (search_limit), którego jeszcze nie ma; reszta działa.",
          "en": "Calibration: this is our approximation, not a replica; the exact replication and comparative tests belong to the replication stage. 10 search results is a preset number. The kernel applies this profile except the search through past conversations (search_limit), which does not exist yet; the rest works."
        }
      }
    ],
    "profile_prefix": {
      "default_level": "normal",
      "header": "What the user has told about themselves. This block does not change from turn to turn while the profile stays the same.",
      "subgraph_line": "[{label}]",
      "item_line": "- {key}: {value}",
      "regions": {
        "minimal": {
          "subgraphs": [
            "preferences"
          ],
          "keys": [
            "preference.style",
            "preference.language"
          ]
        },
        "normal": {
          "subgraphs": [
            "identity",
            "preferences",
            "policies",
            "units"
          ],
          "keys": null
        },
        "detailed": {
          "subgraphs": null,
          "keys": null
        }
      },
      "subgraph_keys": {
        "identity": [],
        "preferences": [
          "preference.style",
          "preference.length",
          "preference.language",
          "preference.adhd_needs"
        ],
        "policies": [],
        "units": [],
        "interests": [],
        "network": []
      }
    },
    "attachments": {
      "text_max_chars": 15000,
      "on_unreadable": "refuse",
      "cut_marker": {
        "en": "[cut: {kept} of {original} characters of {file} were sent; the rest was left out]",
        "pl": "[ucięto: z {file} wysłano {kept} z {original} znaków; resztę pominięto]",
        "nl": "[ingekort: van {file} zijn {kept} van {original} tekens verzonden; de rest is weggelaten]"
      },
      "unreadable_error": {
        "en": "the attachment {file} cannot be read, so nothing was sent. Fix the file or set chat_attachment_on_unreadable to send_with_warning.",
        "pl": "nie można odczytać załącznika {file}, więc nic nie wysłano. Napraw plik albo ustaw chat_attachment_on_unreadable na send_with_warning.",
        "nl": "de bijlage {file} kan niet worden gelezen, dus er is niets verzonden. Herstel het bestand of zet chat_attachment_on_unreadable op send_with_warning."
      },
      "unreadable_marker": {
        "en": "[the attachment {file} could not be read and is not included]",
        "pl": "[załącznika {file} nie dało się odczytać i nie został dołączony]",
        "nl": "[de bijlage {file} kon niet worden gelezen en is niet bijgevoegd]"
      }
    }
  },
  "value_schema": {
    "type": "object",
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "required": [
      "context_order",
      "orders"
    ],
    "properties": {
      "context_order": {
        "type": "string",
        "x-setting": "/context_order",
        "x-consumer": "chat_engine",
        "description": "Name of the active order; must be a key of orders. Per-send option context_order and config key chat_context_order override it. Preset: stability."
      },
      "orders": {
        "type": "object",
        "x-setting": "/orders",
        "x-consumer": "chat_engine",
        "additionalProperties": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "system",
              "profile",
              "rules",
              "memory",
              "project",
              "history",
              "graph"
            ]
          }
        },
        "description": "Named orders over the classes system (S0), profile (the stable part about the user), rules (the rules about the user), memory (S1), project (S2), history (S3), graph (S4). Active task and the question (S5) are always last."
      },
      "selector_profiles": {
        "type": "array",
        "x-setting": "/selector_profiles",
        "x-consumer": "chat_engine",
        "description": "Presets of the context selector, listed as the view kind selector_profiles (node selector_profile:<id>). A profile is a bundle of existing knobs; the kernel applies the table from work item M1-K1a on (search_limit excepted: there is no search over past conversations yet). Chosen by ChatOptions.selector_profile, then the turn value context.profile, then the scope chain (rules and the setting selector_profile); none chosen = the settings as they are.",
        "items": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "id",
            "label",
            "order",
            "status"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "id": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1,
              "description": "Name of the profile; the address of its node is selector_profile:<id>."
            },
            "label": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": [
                "pl",
                "en"
              ],
              "properties": {
                "pl": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "minLength": 1
                },
                "en": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "minLength": 1
                }
              },
              "additionalProperties": false
            },
            "why": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": [
                "pl",
                "en"
              ],
              "properties": {
                "pl": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "minLength": 1
                },
                "en": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "minLength": 1
                }
              },
              "additionalProperties": false
            },
            "order": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1,
              "description": "A key of orders."
            },
            "sources": {
              "type": "object",
              "description": "Which classes of context the profile reads: profile, rules, memory, project, history, graph, search, kb. true = read (the conversation toggles still apply); false = not read.",
              "additionalProperties": {
                "type": "boolean"
              }
            },
            "breadth": {
              "type": "object",
              "description": "nodes: how many graph nodes (null = setting graph_memory_max_nodes); search_limit: how many search results; history_window: how many last messages (null = the whole conversation).",
              "properties": {
                "nodes": {
                  "type": [
                    "integer",
                    "null"
                  ]
                },
                "search_limit": {
                  "type": [
                    "integer",
                    "null"
                  ]
                },
                "history_window": {
                  "type": [
                    "integer",
                    "null"
                  ]
                }
              },
              "additionalProperties": false
            },
            "depth": {
              "type": "object",
              "description": "hops: how many links from the focus the graph selection follows (null = setting graph_memory_depth).",
              "properties": {
                "hops": {
                  "type": [
                    "integer",
                    "null"
                  ]
                }
              },
              "additionalProperties": false
            },
            "representation": {
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ],
              "description": "A preset of the guardian profile representation (raw, denoised, lean, guardian, mixed); null = setting chat_representation."
            },
            "flow": {
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ],
              "description": "A flow of the guardian profile context_io (plain, graph_out, graph_in, graph_io); null = setting chat_flow."
            },
            "budget_tokens": {
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null"
              ],
              "description": "A token budget of the profile’s own; null = none of its own."
            },
            "status": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1,
              "description": "preset or calibration (a user’s own profile may use its own word)."
            },
            "note": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": [
                "pl",
                "en"
              ],
              "properties": {
                "pl": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "minLength": 1
                },
                "en": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "minLength": 1
                }
              },
              "additionalProperties": false
            }
          },
          "additionalProperties": true
        }
      },
      "profile_prefix": {
        "type": "object",
        "x-setting": "/profile_prefix",
        "x-consumer": "chat_engine",
        "description": "Recipe of the class profile: default_level (used when profile_detail_level names none of the regions), header, subgraph_line ({label}), item_line ({key}, {value}), regions {level: {subgraphs: [ids] or null = every subgraph with an order_for_prefix, keys: [keys] or null = every key}} and subgraph_keys {subgraph id: [keys of the onboarding layers that belong to it]}. Only values the person set themselves are rendered, in a fixed order, with no time stamps or counters. Detail levels of a goal (context_goal_cues) are not read: they change from turn to turn and would change the prefix.",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": [
          "default_level",
          "header",
          "subgraph_line",
          "item_line",
          "regions",
          "subgraph_keys"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "default_level": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          },
          "header": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          },
          "subgraph_line": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          },
          "item_line": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          },
          "regions": {
            "type": "object",
            "additionalProperties": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": [
                "subgraphs",
                "keys"
              ],
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "subgraphs": {
                  "type": [
                    "array",
                    "null"
                  ],
                  "items": {
                    "type": "string"
                  }
                },
                "keys": {
                  "type": [
                    "array",
                    "null"
                  ],
                  "items": {
                    "type": "string"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "subgraph_keys": {
            "type": "object",
            "additionalProperties": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "attachments": {
        "type": "object",
        "x-setting": "/attachments",
        "x-consumer": "chat_engine",
        "description": "Attached files: text_max_chars is the preset of the setting chat_attachment_max_chars (characters of a text file sent to the model; 0 = no limit); on_unreadable is the preset of chat_attachment_on_unreadable (refuse | send_with_warning); cut_marker, unreadable_error and unreadable_marker are the words ({file}, {kept}, {original}) in en, pl, nl."
      }
    }
  }
}
